<h2 id="includes">What This Service Includes</h2>
<p>This is a full program build, not a single deliverable. It covers the clinical protocol, the staff who deliver it, the documentation that makes it defensible, and the billing structure that makes it sustainable. Everything is developed specifically for your practice — your space, your staff, your patient population, and your state's requirements.</p>

<h3>Program Components</h3>
<div class="dash-list">
  <div class="dash-list-item">A documented preparation and delivery protocol, specified by indication</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Staff training to competency, with sign-off records</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">AAAHC-aligned policies and procedures written for your practice</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Billing and coding guidance appropriate to your state and payer mix</div>
</div>

<h3>What You Retain Control Of</h3>
<p>You keep full clinical authority. Regenitiva builds and maintains the operational structure around the program — we don't practice medicine, and we don't take that decision away from you or your team.</p>

<blockquote>"We were referring these patients out for years. Now we're the ones who can help them." — Physiatrist, California practice</blockquote>

<h2 id="process">How We Build It</h2>
<p>The build runs in four stages, typically over six to ten weeks depending on your state's requirements and how much clinical infrastructure already exists in your practice.</p>

<div class="numbered-steps">
  <div class="numbered-step">
    <span class="numbered-step-badge">1</span>
    <div>
      <div class="numbered-step-title">Assessment</div>
      <p class="numbered-step-body">We review your space, staff, patient population, and state requirements to scope the program.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="numbered-step">
    <span class="numbered-step-badge">2</span>
    <div>
      <div class="numbered-step-title">Protocol &amp; Documentation</div>
      <p class="numbered-step-body">We write the clinical protocol, policies, and procedures specific to your practice.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="numbered-step">
    <span class="numbered-step-badge">3</span>
    <div>
      <div class="numbered-step-title">Training</div>
      <p class="numbered-step-body">Your whole team trains remotely, on your own equipment, until signed off to competency.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="numbered-step">
    <span class="numbered-step-badge">4</span>
    <div>
      <div class="numbered-step-title">Launch &amp; Support</div>
      <p class="numbered-step-body">You begin treating patients with ongoing auditing and outcome tracking in place.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<figure>
  <div style="width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16/9; background: var(--rg-stone-300); border-radius: var(--rg-radius-md);"></div>
  <figcaption>Remote training is delivered directly in your procedure rooms, on your own equipment.</figcaption>
</figure>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-label">Why this matters</div>
  <p class="callout-body">Programs built without documented training and sign-off records are the ones that don't hold up under a payer audit. We build the record as we build the program, not after something goes wrong.</p>
</div>

<h2 id="compliance">Compliance &amp; Documentation</h2>
<p>Every program includes a complete documentation set, maintained as standards change. Read more about our full approach on the <a href="/compliance">Compliance &amp; Operations</a> page.</p>

<h4>Documentation Set</h4>
<div class="dash-list">
  <div class="dash-list-item">Clinical protocol and technique standards</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Staff competency and training records</div>
  <div class="dash-list-item">Internal audit schedule and quality management plan</div>
</div>

<h2 id="timeline">Timeline &amp; Investment</h2>
<p>Every engagement is scoped to the practice, so there isn't a list price. A single physician adding a service line is a different build than a multi-site group standardizing across locations.</p>

<h3>Typical Timeline</h3>
<p>Most practices are treating patients within six to ten weeks of kickoff. We'll give you a specific figure and a realistic schedule during the assessment — <a href="/contact">start a conversation</a> to get started.</p>

